.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DRIVER_UNREGISTER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm driver_unregister
.Nd remove a driver from a bus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/driver.h
.Ft int
.Fn driver_unregister "struct driver *drv"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn driver_unregister
function removes a device driver from the system.
.Pp
It performs the following actions:
.Bl -enum
.It
Iterates over all devices on the driver's bus.
.It
For any device bound to this driver, invokes the
.Fn detach
callback (if present) and clears the device's driver binding.
.It
Removes the driver from the bus's list of registered drivers.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn driver_unregister
function returns 0 on success.
.Pp
It returns -1 if authentication fails or arguments are invalid.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr driver_register 9 ,
.Xr driver_detach 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn driver_unregister
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
